# CITATION.cff — makes GitHub's "Cite this repository" button work and feeds
# Zenodo metadata on future mints. The concept DOI below cites the living work
# (always resolves to the latest archived version); cite a version DOI only to
# pin a release (v3.11.6: 10.5281/zenodo.23303470).
#
# NOTE (2026-10-11): the authors list currently carries the human author only.
# The README credits Claude models as co-creators; whether the FORMAL citation
# record lists them is the founder's standing decision (flagged at the first
# mint, Custos brief 1757) — amend here and in the Zenodo record when ruled.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this template or build on its methodology, please cite it
  using the metadata below. The concept DOI (10.5281/zenodo.23303469)
  always resolves to the latest archived release; cite a version DOI to
  pin the exact release you used.
title: "ADRs for AI: Human-AI Collaboration Template A"
abstract: >-
  The canonical template of ADRs for AI (ADRs4AI) — git-native tooling for deliberative
  programming: human-AI collaboration in which decisions are first-class,
  durable artifacts. Humans and AI agents co-author Architectural
  Deliberation Records (ADRs) and seeds in a question-and-answer grammar
  that tooling can parse; every open question carries a reasoned,
  attributed recommendation, so deciding starts from carried reasoning
  rather than a blank page; inbox and crew protocols extend one
  deliberation record across multi-agent, multi-vendor teams. The
  template's own development record is the first specimen: the method
  ships demonstrated in the substrate it was built with.
keywords:
  - "human-AI collaboration"
  - "deliberative programming"
  - "architectural deliberation records"
  - "architecture decision records"
  - "AI agents"
  - "multi-agent coordination"
  - "software engineering methodology"
  - "knowledge management"
authors:
  - family-names: "Lumbroso"
    given-names: "Jérémie"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23303469
repository-code: "https://github.com/ADRs4AI/human-ai-collaboration-template-A"
license: MIT
